# Day 8: Wazuh basics

## What I learned
- SIEM collects security logs from agents and generates structured alerts.
- Wazuh architecture consists of 3 core components: Agent, Server (Manager), and Dashboard.
- Alert severity levels range from 0 to 15 (lower levels indicate informational events, 12+ indicate critical security threats).
- Navigated threat hunting fields: rule.description, rule.level, agent.name, and timestamp.

## What I did
- Reviewed Wazuh SIEM deployment workflow and WM agent registration steps.
- Analyzed alert level classification and dashboard log visualization technigues.
